<clickhouse>
  <!--
    Cap ClickHouse's internal system_logs so a small self-hosted instance
    does not blow up disk usage. Langfuse only needs query/part history,
    not weeks of telemetry on itself.

    NOTE: A system table whose default config.xml entry already specifies an
    <engine> cannot take a separate <ttl> here. ClickHouse refuses to start:

      Code: 36. DB::Exception: If 'engine' is specified for system table,
      TTL parameters should be specified directly inside 'engine' and 'ttl'
      setting doesn't make sense. (BAD_ARGUMENTS)

    In 25.7.3.13 that applies to opentelemetry_span_log, which is therefore
    omitted below. Before adding a table here, check whether the stock
    /etc/clickhouse-server/config.xml defines an engine for it, by running
    sed over that file inside the image and looking for an engine element in
    the table's block.

    (Careful: a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment, so command
    flags cannot be written out here. ClickHouse rejects the whole file with
    a SAXParseException if you try.)

    Verified 2026-08-17 against clickhouse-server 25.7.3.13 (aarch64): this
    file starts cleanly ("Ready for connections"); re-adding
    opentelemetry_span_log makes the server exit 36 on startup.
  -->
  <text_log>                <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 3 DAY DELETE</ttl></text_log>
  <trace_log>               <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 3 DAY DELETE</ttl></trace_log>
  <metric_log>              <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 3 DAY DELETE</ttl></metric_log>
  <asynchronous_metric_log> <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 3 DAY DELETE</ttl></asynchronous_metric_log>
  <latency_log>             <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 3 DAY DELETE</ttl></latency_log>
  <query_log>               <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 7 DAY DELETE</ttl></query_log>
  <part_log>                <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 7 DAY DELETE</ttl></part_log>
  <query_metric_log>        <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 3 DAY DELETE</ttl></query_metric_log>
</clickhouse>
